{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"IMPLEMENTED AND VERIFIED. Gerrit change 1102, commit 18dda0f27, LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1.\n\nsrc/rebar/llm/model_classes.py, 178 LOC. config.py UNTOUCHED at 777 (the one-way import edge holds:\nmodel_classes imports infer_provider/DEFAULT_MODEL/VERIFIER_DEFAULT_MODEL from config; config does\nnot import it back).\n\nHELD-OUT TDD. 16 tests authored before the code; ONE (the happy path) given to the implementer, the\nother 15 physically removed from the worktree. All 15 passed on the implementer's FIRST attempt.\nThen six behavioural mutations, each asserted-as-applied before the red check:\n\n  frontier default -> sonnet ................................. CAUGHT\n  skip the api_key check on fallback ENTRIES ................. CAUGHT\n  allow a NESTED fallback .................................... CAUGHT\n  env override clobbers sibling fields ....................... CAUGHT\n  double-prefix an already-qualified model ................... CAUGHT\n  unknown class silently defaults instead of raising ......... CAUGHT\n\nSuite: 8175 passed, 74 skipped, 0 failed (0:26:31) — the prior 8159 plus exactly these 16.\n\nONE DEFECT THE BEHAVIOURAL ORACLE COULD NOT CATCH, worth recording as the lesson from this ticket.\ndocs/env-vars.md is DERIVED: scripts/gen_env_registry.py scans src/rebar for LITERAL env-var name\nstrings and CI fails the build if the committed copy drifts. The first implementation built the nine\nnames with an f-string, which is fine Python but INVISIBLE to the scanner — regenerating produced\nonly 'model_classes.py:83 — os.environ.get(<non-literal>)', filing the nine vars under 'name not\nstatically determinable' instead of documenting them. 16/16 tests passed and six mutations were\ncaught, and the change would STILL have failed CI. Structural constraints (module size, derived-file\nregeneration) live outside the behavioural net; that is why they belong in the implementer brief. I\nbriefed module size and missed the doc generator — one round-trip.\n\nFixed by spelling the nine names out as literals, with a comment saying WHY so nobody tidies it back\ninto an f-string. Verified properly: the nine now appear attributed to model_classes.py, the\n<non-literal> line is gone, and REGENERATING PRODUCES BYTE-IDENTICAL OUTPUT (my first idempotency\ncheck was wrong — I diffed against HEAD, which of course differs by the nine new rows; the real\ncheck is snapshot-then-regenerate-then-compare).\n\nTHREE UNDER-SPECIFICATIONS the implementer flagged, resolved here so cc33 does not re-litigate them:\n1. A slot present but with model missing/empty falls back to the class default rather than erroring.\n   Erroring would force every configured slot to repeat model even when it only wants to set provider.\n2. A bare model whose provider cannot be inferred is returned UNPREFIXED, mirroring the existing\n   _pai_model precedent in anthropic_model.py. Same as today's behaviour, so no existing config moves.\n3. An empty-string env var is treated as UNSET (falls through to table/default), matching the rest of\n   rebar's env layer."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785486608946872001,"uuid":"217a6271-d007-4c6e-98f5-a64ff51e7d4a"}